              "text": "rule ordinary_bza_vote_threshold\n  id detroit.article_ii.50_2_78.ordinary_threshold\n  source §50-2-78\n    \"The concurring vote of a majority of the members of the Board of Zoning Appeals shall be necessary to reverse or adjust any order, requirement, decision, or determination of any administrative official, or to decide in favor of the applicant on any matter upon which the Board is required to pass under this chapter, or to grant a variance in this chapter.\"\n  given all\n    decision: BoardDecision\n    decision is decided by DetroitBZA\n    decision concerns an ordinary BZA matter\n  conclude constitutive\n    decision requires concurrence from a majority of authorized board members",
